Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-13-2000||07:30 PM||||  I had mentioned in an earlier post somwhere that my car runs fine at around 70 degrees F. It starts to warm up after that. What is the normal operating temp for a Fiero 2.8L? I usually run at or around 170 to 185, should I worry if the needle starts to aproach 200 or 220? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Any inf ormation helpful <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  Thanx Bam <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||william_thorniii||03-13-2000||08:15 PM||||Bam-Bam,<P>200-220 is not a problem what so ever.  In fact the electric fan does not kick in until temperatures in that region are detected.  If sitting idle you should be able to watch your temperature rise until you hear a noise from the front compartment.  After that temperature should drop steadily until back down around 175-180 when the fan kicks back off.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||03-13-2000||09:30 PM||||  Thanks for that information, it's helpful <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Also, where is the sending unit for the fan located. I recently changed the one for the guage. Is there a different one for the fan? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>  Thanx, BAM-BAM <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> ||||reg||10
